    oe:aboutDisease oed:trigeminal_neuralgia ;
    oe:answerText "Trigeminal neuralgia is characterized classically by recurrent, evocable, unilateral brief, electric, shocklike pains with an abrupt onset and cessation that affects one or more divisions of the trigeminal nerve. In recent years, the classification of trigeminal neuralgia has been updated based on further understanding."^^xsd:string ;
